cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Bioethics Bench, cite the standalone Bioethics Bench manuscript
  when a stable bibliographic citation is available, and identify the exact
  resource or record version used. Record-level citations should include
  record_id, version, and content_hash.
title: "Bioethics Bench"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Alethic Research"
abstract: >-
  A source-grounded, versioned research infrastructure for computational
  bioethics. Bioethics Bench represents bioethical decision problems as
  reconstructable normative research objects with explicit policy candidates,
  provenance and warrant information, benchmark stipulations, controlled
  representations, version lineage, review state, and separable task and
  evaluation layers.
repository-code: "https://github.com/alethicresearch/bioethics-bench"
url: "https://bioethicsbench.com"
keywords:
  - bioethics
  - computational bioethics
  - normative computation
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
version: "development"
